<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Investing in a certified storm shelter is one of the most critical safety upgrades for any North Texas home. In 2026, residential storm shelter installations across Sherman, Denison, and Grayson County typically range between <strong>$4,500 and $9,500</strong>, with qualified homeowners eligible for up to <strong>$3,000 in matching rebates</strong> through county emergency management programs.</p><p>The total cost depends primarily on shelter type (above-ground steel vs. underground concrete vs. garage in-floor), capacity, foundation modifications, and accessibility features.</p></div></div></section>
