<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Cost Factors for North Texas Storm Shelters</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Several key variables determine the final turnkey price of your storm shelter installation:</p><ul><li><strong>Shelter Type & Materials:</strong> Modular 10-gauge and 1/4-inch steel safe rooms offer rapid indoor assembly, while pre-cast 6,000 PSI concrete underground units require heavy excavation equipment and crane placement.</li><li><strong>Slab Thickness & Anchoring:</strong> Above-ground safe rooms require a minimum 4-inch, 2,500+ PSI reinforced concrete slab. Post-installed Hilti anchor bolts must meet strict embedment depths.</li><li><strong>Excavation & High Water Table:</strong> Underground installations in clay soil require proper sealing, drainage bedding, and anti-buoyancy considerations.</li><li><strong>Accessibility Upgrades:</strong> Wider 36-inch doors, wheelchair ramps, and internal bench seating add modest custom fabrication costs.</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">How the Grayson County 50% Rebate Reduces Your Cost</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>The Grayson County Office of Emergency Management periodically administers the FEMA Hazard Mitigation Grant Program (HMGP) Residential Safe Room Rebate. Under this program, approved homeowners receive a 50% reimbursement (up to a maximum of $3,000) for installing an EF5-rated safe room.</p><p>Important requirements include obtaining pre-approval prior to installation, using a certified installer compliant with FEMA P-320 guidelines, pulling appropriate municipal permits in Sherman or Denison, and registering the finished shelter.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Above-Ground vs. Underground: Cost and Practicality</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>While underground concrete bunkers have traditionally been popular in rural Texas, above-ground steel safe rooms have become the modern standard across North Texas residential subdivisions. Above-ground units provide instant access without navigating wet, steep stairs during severe weather, make evacuation effortless for elderly family members and pets, and completely eliminate flooding or spider/insect infiltration risks.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Return on Investment & Home Equity Value</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>In tornado-prone North Texas markets, an engineered storm shelter is a major selling point that increases buyer appeal and resale equity. Appraisers frequently credit certified safe rooms at or near full replacement value, and some insurance providers offer policy discounts for certified storm mitigation features.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#EAF5FB;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does a typical 6-person storm shelter cost installed?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">A standard 6-person above-ground steel safe room averages $4,800 to $6,500 installed, including slab anchoring and local permit filing. With the Grayson County rebate, the net cost drops to $2,400 to $3,500.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Does the estimate include permits and installation?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes. Our written quotes are 100% turnkey, covering site delivery, precision slab cutting or excavation, certified anchor hardware, municipal permit filing, and county registry documentation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Can I install an above-ground safe room in an existing home?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes. Our modular steel safe rooms are designed to fit through standard 30-inch doorways and assemble panel-by-panel inside existing garages, basements, or ground-floor interior rooms.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Are underground storm shelters more expensive than above-ground safe rooms?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Turnkey costs are comparable. While pre-cast concrete units have slightly lower fabrication costs, the excavation, crane rental, and soil haul-away bring the total installed price to $5,200 - $8,800.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How can I apply for the Grayson County safe room rebate?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Contact the Grayson County Office of Emergency Management or speak with our team. We provide the certified engineering documentation and quote specifications required for your grant application.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
